                <p>The Secretary of the Treasury believes that, before the proposed policies for the
                    Far East are finally approved, the proposed levels of military and economic
                    programs should be reviewed in the light of (a) the priority of financing the
                    present and proposed programs for the Far East in relation to programs for other
                    foreign areas and to programs for domestic security, and (b) the over-all
                    objective of achieving a balanced budget.</p>
